quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  39,75,"And, (O Beloved,) you will see the angels all around the Throne in circles glorifying the Lord with His praise, and the judgment will be given amongst (all) the people with truth and justice and it will be announced: ‘All praise belongs to Allah alone, the Sustainer of all the worlds.’"
  40,1,"Ha, Mim. (Only Allah and the Messenger [blessings and peace be upon him] know the real meaning.)"
  40,2,"The revelation of this Book is from Allah, the Almighty, All-Knowing,"
  40,3,"The Forgiver of sin, the Acceptor of repentance, the Severe in tormenting, the Lord of bounty; there is no God but He; towards Him (all) are to return."
  40,4,No one disputes about the Revelations of Allah except those who do not believe. So let not their moving about (freely) in the cities delude you.
  40,5,"Before them the people of Nuh (Noah) and after them many (other) communities rejected (their Messengers). And every people intended to seize its Messenger (to assassinate or imprison him), and raised dispute through baseless issues to dilute (the influence of) the truth by means of that (dispute). So I seized them (in torment). So how was (My) torment!"
  40,6,"That is how the judgment of your Lord was fulfilled against those who disbelieved. Surely, they are the inmates of Hell."
  40,7,"The angels who are bearing the Throne and those who are around it, (all) glorify their Lord with His praise and believe in Him and pray for forgiveness of the believers (and submit): ‘O our Lord, You encompass everything in (Your) mercy and knowledge. So forgive those who turn to You in repentance and follow Your path and protect them from the torment of Hell."
